/* yywrap for flex scanners whose .l file does not supply one.   flex's own skeleton documents the default as       /* default yywrap function - always treat EOF as an EOF *\/       #define yywrap() 1   but the self-contained skeleton shipped with the EFFO flex leaves it to   the caller, and deansi.l does not define it.  This is that default, as a   real function, so deansi.l itself stays exactly as distributed.   Returning 1 means "no further input file" -- stop at EOF. */int yywrap()    {    return 1;    }